    <text>
        <front>
            <div type="summary">
                <p>
                Warren explains that his anthology has not yet been published. 
                He hopes that the book will came out in the summer.
                He also promises that as soon as the book is published the fee for Frank Prewett's poem included in the book will be forwarded to The Hogarth Press.
                </p>
            </div>
        </front>
        <body>
            <div type="letter">
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                            <placeName key="Q676067">
                                <settlement>Braintree</settlement>
                                <region>Essex</region>
                            </placeName>
                        <date when="1946-04-20">20 April 1946</date>
                    </dateline>
                    <address>
                            <addrLine><orgName key="Q1623362">The Hogarth Press</orgName>,</addrLine>
                            <addrLine>37 Mecklenburgh Sq. WC.</addrLine>
                    </address>
                    <salute>Dear Sirs,</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    In reply to<lb/>
                    your enquiry concerning my<lb/> 
                    anthology <title><choice><orig>the good life</orig><reg>The Good Life: 
                                An Anthology of the Life and Work of the Countryside, 
                                in Prose and Poetry.</reg></choice></title> (<orgName key="Q5422976">Eyre<lb/> 
                    &amp; Spottiswoode</orgName>), this has not<lb/> 
                    yet been published. <note><p>The book was originally planned for publication in 1945, 
                            according to Warren's correspondence with The Hogarth Press on 12 September 1944.</p></note> For<lb/> 
                    reasons which will be all too<lb/> 
                    familiar to you, it has been<lb/> 
                    continually held up. It is<lb/> 
                    hoped, however, that the book<lb/> 
                    will appear this summer; ,<note><p>The book was sucessfully published that year.</p></note><lb/> 
                    of course, as soon as it is<lb/> 
                    published, the fee for <persName key="Q1257757">Mr. Frank<lb/> 
                    Prewett</persName>'s poem
                    <note><p>Poem refers to Frank Prewett's poem "Be Kind to Animals", 
                            which was once published by The Hogarth Press and Warren included this poem in his anthology The Good Life.</p></note>
                    will be forwarded<pb/> 
                    to you.
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <salute>Yours faithfully,</salute>
                    <signed>C. Henry Warren</signed>
                    <address>
                        <addrLine>Timbers</addrLine>
                        <addrLine>Finchingfield</addrLine>
                        <addrLine>N. Braintree</addrLine>
                        <addrLine>Essex.</addrLine>
                    </address>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
